      "problem": "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =20+2 \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{22}.\n$$",
